id: pm-gh1614
title: "GH-1614: keep typed SDK data literal across CLI sentinel inputs"
description: "GitHub https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1614 reports typed PmClient fields consuming CLI sentinels. A sandboxed current-source Node24 probe with closed stdin reproduces description '-' becoming empty and assignee 'none' being removed. Typed integrations can silently rewrite provider payloads. Audit create/update/append and separate literal typed input from explicit CLI stdin, file and clear transport syntax, retaining documented unset APIs and CLI compatibility."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T17:43:51.501Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T00:30:30.380Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-28T00:30:29.584Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T00:30:29.584Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Literal SDK text fields preserve sentinel spellings through create/update/append; SDK data calls do not implicitly consume stdin or read files; Explicit typed clear/unset and existing CLI transport semantics retain focused conformance tests
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Programmatic create/update/append and bulk mutation values preserve dash, none, null and file-like strings as domain data. Public SDK policy helpers preserve explicit CLI stdin and clear syntax, with literal decoded JSON and migration documentation."
expected_result: "SDK mutation strings round-trip without implicit input or unintended clearing, while CLI transport and explicit unset remain correct."
actual_result: "All11518 tests pass; exact coverage is100/100/100/100 with67333 lines,54837 branches,14654 functions and71204 statements covered. Both linked test groups pass. Packed npm and Bun consumers verify both public entrypoints, two input modes and five typed no-write refusals; nine-package npx/bunx smoke passes. Typecheck, version, security, token and static component checks pass after typed graph/context repairs. Final composite static and exact-head hosted review remain delivery gates."
